# Playwright's text snapshots are compared byte for byte.
#
# `compareText` in playwright-core reads the committed file into a Buffer,
# decodes it as UTF-8 and asks `expected === actual` — there is no line-ending
# normalisation anywhere in that path. This repo is developed on Windows with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and deliberately leaves the working copy CRLF (see the
# root `.gitattributes`), so without this line a fresh clone would check these
# files out with CRLF while the spec captures LF from the browser and the
# script, and `dev-usage-guardrail.spec.ts` would fail every line at once on a
# tree nobody had touched.
#
# It does not reproduce on the machine that wrote the snapshots: Playwright
# writes them with LF and they are only rewritten by a checkout, so the failure
# waits for the next clone. CI is Linux and would never see it either.
dev-usage-guardrail.spec.ts-snapshots/* text eol=lf
